¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd he said, Behold, I make a covenant: before all thy people I will do marvels, such as have not been done in all the earth, nor in any nation: and all the people among which thou art shall see the work of the LORD: for it is a terrible thing that I will do with thee.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶Observe thou that which I command thee this day: behold, I drive out before thee the Amorite, and the Canaanite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, and the Hivite, and the Jebusite.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘Take heed to thyself, lest thou make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land whither thou goest, lest it be for a snare in the midst of thee:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQbut ye shall destroy their altars, break their images, and cut down their groves:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[for thou shalt worship no other god: for the LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ·lest thou make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land, and they go a whoring after their gods, and do sacrifice unto their gods, and one call thee, and thou eat of his sacrifice;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“and thou take of their daughters unto thy sons, and their daughters go a whoring after their gods, and make thy sons go a whoring after their gods.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ$Thou shalt make thee no molten gods.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter"«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÀThe feast of unleavened bread shalt thou keep. Seven days thou shalt eat unleavened bread, as I commanded thee, in the time of the month Abib: for in the month Abib thou camest out from Egypt.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter"«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAll that openeth the matrix is mine; and every firstling among thy cattle, whether ox or sheep, that is male.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÎBut the firstling of an ass thou shalt redeem with a lamb: and if thou redeem him not, then shalt thou break his neck. All the firstborn of thy sons thou shalt redeem. And none shall appear before me empty.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter"«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpSix days thou shalt work, but on the seventh day thou shalt rest: in earing time and in harvest thou shalt rest.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter"«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd thou shalt observe the feast of weeks, of the firstfruits of wheat harvest, and the feast of ingathering at the year's end.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\Thrice in the year shall all your menchildren appear before the Lord GOD, the God of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¸For I will cast out the nations before thee, and enlarge thy borders: neither shall any man desire thy land, when thou shalt go up to appear before the LORD thy God thrice in the year.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter"«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThou shalt not offer the blood of my sacrifice with leaven; neither shall the sacrifice of the feast of the passover be left unto the morning.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThe first of the firstfruits of thy land thou shalt bring unto the house of the LORD thy God. Thou shalt not seethe a kid in his mother's milk.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter"«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠAnd the LORD said unto Moses, Write thou these words: for after the tenor of these words I have made a covenant with thee and with Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´And he was there with the LORD forty days and forty nights; he did neither eat bread, nor drink water. And he wrote upon the tables the words of the covenant, the ten commandments.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter"«first_verseªlast_verse#¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÛAnd it came to pass, when Moses came down from mount Sinai with the two tables of testimony in Moses' hand, when he came down from the mount, that Moses wist not that the skin of his face shone while he talked with him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒAnd when Aaron and all the children of Israel saw Moses, behold, the skin of his face shone; and they were afraid to come nigh him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{And Moses called unto them; and Aaron and all the rulers of the congregation returned unto him: and Moses talked with them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰And afterward all the children of Israel came nigh: and he gave them in commandment all that the LORD had spoken with him in mount Sinai.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFAnd till Moses had done speaking with them, he put a vail on his face.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶But when Moses went in before the LORD to speak with him, he took the vail off, until he came out. And he came out, and spake unto the children of Israel that which he was commanded.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥And the children of Israel saw the face of Moses, that the skin of Moses' face shone: and Moses put the vail upon his face again, until he went in to speak with him.¦layout ªlast_verse#